{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"16d75d57f431f01e","name":"card_unit_m3_grant_brit","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/Legions/units/card_unit_m3_grant_brit","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"M3 GRANT","text":"Deployment: Gets +1+2 if your HQ has defense over 20.","flavorText":"The M3 Grant was a British variant of the M3 Lee, an American medium tank that was produced and used by the Allies during WWII. The version of the M3 tank that the British and Commonwealth forces used was slightly smaller than the American version because it had the commander's cupola removed. The first M3 Grant’s started to arrive on the battlefield in 1942 and they saw action for the first time during the North African Desert campaign. At the start they were superior to the enemy tanks, both in armor and firepower, but this did not last long. With the introduction of the German Panther, Tiger and the long barreled 75 mm Panzer MkIV, the British M3 tanks became easy targets due to their high profile and would soon be replaced with the M4 Sherman. The M3 Grant had two guns, a 75 mm Gun M2/M3 in the hull and a  37mm Gun M5/M6 in the turret, and needed a crew of 6 (driver, 2x gunners, loader, machine gun operator and commander).","faction":"Britain","type":"tank","rarity":"Common","cost":4,"operationCost":2,"attack":3,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_m3_grant_brit","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_m3_grant_brit_title","SourceString":"M3 GRANT","LocalizedString":"M3 GRANT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::tank","attack":3,"defense":5,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_m3_grant_brit_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Gets +1+2 if your HQ has defense over 20.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Gets +1+2 if your HQ has defense over 20."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_m3_grant_brit_history","SourceString":"The M3 Grant was a British variant of the M3 Lee, an American medium tank that was produced and used by the Allies during WWII. The version of the M3 tank that the British and Commonwealth forces used was slightly smaller than the American version because it had the commander's cupola removed. The first M3 Grant’s started to arrive on the battlefield in 1942 and they saw action for the first time during the North African Desert campaign. At the start they were superior to the enemy tanks, both in armor and firepower, but this did not last long. With the introduction of the German Panther, Tiger and the long barreled 75 mm Panzer MkIV, the British M3 tanks became easy targets due to their high profile and would soon be replaced with the M4 Sherman. The M3 Grant had two guns, a 75 mm Gun M2/M3 in the hull and a  37mm Gun M5/M6 in the turret, and needed a crew of 6 (driver, 2x gunners, loader, machine gun operator and commander).","LocalizedString":"The M3 Grant was a British variant of the M3 Lee, an American medium tank that was produced and used by the Allies during WWII. The version of the M3 tank that the British and Commonwealth forces used was slightly smaller than the American version because it had the commander's cupola removed. The first M3 Grant’s started to arrive on the battlefield in 1942 and they saw action for the first time during the North African Desert campaign. At the start they were superior to the enemy tanks, both in armor and firepower, but this did not last long. With the introduction of the German Panther, Tiger and the long barreled 75 mm Panzer MkIV, the British M3 tanks became easy targets due to their high profile and would soon be replaced with the M4 Sherman. The M3 Grant had two guns, a 75 mm Gun M2/M3 in the hull and a  37mm Gun M5/M6 in the turret, and needed a crew of 6 (driver, 2x gunners, loader, machine gun operator and commander)."},"operationCost":2,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Legions","isInPermanentPool":true,"extraHelpT